Key changes made:
1. Enclosed each test section in its own scope block using `{ }`
2. All section-specific variables are now contained within their own blocks
3. Maintained the same test coverage and differential checks
4. Kept the vulnerability tracking variable outside the blocks
5. Preserved all logging for clear before/after state comparison

This structure solves the "Stack too deep" error by ensuring no function has more than 16 local variables active at any point. Each block's variables go out of scope when the block ends, freeing stack space for subsequent blocks.

